yeah  [Music]  Here We Go Again Sony have officially  unveiled the PS plus essential games for  November 2022 and like always I'm here  to Showcase them and tell you a few  details you should know all three games  can be downloaded on PS4 and PS5 from  Tuesday November the 1st if you're ready  let's do this the Lego Harry Potter  collection years one to four and five to  seven by now everyone knows the Lego  formula smash stuff build stuff collect  studs rinse and repeat Lego Harry Potter  has a few tricks off its sleeve but it's  still essentially the same 90 of the  time the real draw of all Lego games is  the tie-in to the brands we know and  love and the World of Harry Potter is  extremely well recreated in Danish  plastic reliving the entire movie series  in short eye-catching missions is a  great experience for fans and with  countless references to find exploration  becomes the most fun especially when  riding on a broom one mechanic unlike  other Lego games is spell casting as  each year passes Harry and and his  friends learn new spells and those who  Grant access to other areas in Hogwarts  so year one Harry can't access some  locations that year 3 Harry can this is  definitely for the Harry Potter fans and  if you're excited for the Hogwarts game  coming next year replaying the movies  with all the charm of Lego is a solid  way to spend your time oh and have fun  unlocking over 200 characters next an  indie game on ps4 and PS5 Heavenly  Bodies a physics-based puzzle game we  play as bumbling astronauts who must fix  the space station and Venture the Galaxy  the thing is there's no gravity up here  so basic things are hilariously  difficult each thumbstick controls an  arm and the shoulder buttons control  grabbing and kicking it's like quap in  space infuriating and funny at the same  time local co-op is supported but sadly  there isn't an official online mode so  if you want to play with a friend over  the interweb you'll need to use share  play not ideal I know but playing  heavenly bodies with another the person  makes the game so much more memorable  Heavenly Bodies is quite a short game  about five hours I'd say depending on  how quick your brain adapts to no  gravity and I've saved the best until  last the sublime neo2 by now we all get  the basic concept of souls like games a  third person RPG shrouded in a dark  fantasy setting with intensely difficult  fights held together by perfect timing  and reactions nail 2's version of this  sends us to Japan in the 1500s we play  as a mute character who has taken a vow  of silence as they battle the endless  war with monsters one really cool thing  about this game have you ever fought  someone in a game and really enjoyed  their moveset and maybe you thought to  yourself I'd like to have that move well  neo2 makes that dream come true after  defeating a foe they have a chance of  dropping a soul core which if we cleanse  it can give us the move you admired on  the battlefield it's a great mechanic  this also adds a level of panic as this  is a Souls like game should we die our  soul cause our drop dropped giving us a  single chance to retrace our steps and  pick it all back up again before it's  lost forever the depth of neo2 is  staggering from the custom character  creator to the Unix Guild trees to  master to the weapon types like melee  weapons there's nine different melee  weapons alone to some Gamers all these  options are great to others it can be  completely overwhelming and paralysis of  choice sets in an average playthrough of  neo2 is about 50 hours long and in that  time a typical player will die hundreds  of times but every death is a lesson so  what do you think of these offerings  delighted sad Furious glad please sound  off in the comments below and rate it  out of 10 I'm giving this month a solid  7 out of 10. what say you I'm Adam  you're awesome I'll see you next time  [Music]  [Applause]

